  "plot": "Linda Liddle carries the weight of a firm while her ego-driven boss, Bradley Preston, coasts on a family name. When their aircraft plunges into the sea, the corporate ladder disintegrates. Bradley clings to his entitlement as a shield against the heat. Linda realizes her meticulous planning is the only thing keeping them breathing. She watches him flounder, a pathetic shell stripped of his suit. The power dynamic curdles. Linda leans into her simmering resentment; she weaponizes her competence to dominate the man who once patronized her. She demands total submission for a sip of water. The price of his survival is the absolute destruction of his dignity.",
